# Valgrind suppressions for Micro-Vocal Lab (nightly memory-check workflow).
#
# Scope: third-party fontconfig charset caches only. The Slint font stack
# (fontique) asks fontconfig for per-script character sets; fontconfig
# caches those allocations for the process lifetime and frees them only in
# FcFini(), which the font stack never calls — the OS reclaims them at
# exit. Reviewed against the Phase 5 run: 592 B definite + 64 B indirect,
# every record passing through FcCharSetAddChar. First-party code (DSP,
# buffers, app state) is leak-free; this gate stays on real regressions.
{
   fontconfig-charset-cache
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   fun:FcCharSetAddChar
}
